      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "# Getting Started with CloudScale DataStream API\n\n## Prerequisites\n- Python 3.8+ installed\n- API key from the dashboard\n- Basic understanding of REST APIs\n\n## Installation\n1. Install the SDK via pip: `pip install cloudscale-datastream`\n2. Initialize your client with your API key: `client = CloudScaleDataStream(api_key=\"your_key\")`\n3. Verify the connection with a simple test request: `client.health_check()`\n\n## Quick Start Example\n- Create a data stream: `stream = client.create_stream(name=\"my_stream\")`\n- Push data to the stream: `stream.push({\"timestamp\": 123456, \"value\": 42})`\n- Retrieve data from the stream: `data = stream.get_records(limit=10)`\n\n## Best Practices\n- Always use environment variables for API keys\n- Implement retry logic for transient failures\n- Monitor stream latency using the built-in metrics endpoint\n\nThis guide provides a solid foundation for developers to start using CloudScale DataStream immediately.",
