      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "# Getting Started with CloudScale DataStream API\n\n## Prerequisites and Setup\n- Ensure you have Python 3.8 or higher installed on your development machine.\n- Obtain a valid API key from the CloudScale Dashboard console.\n- Familiarize yourself with basic REST API concepts and HTTP status codes.\n\n## Installation and Configuration\n1. Install the official SDK using pip: `pip install cloudscale-datastream`.\n2. Create a new virtual environment to isolate dependencies.\n3. Initialize the client object with your API key: `client = CloudScaleDataStream(api_key=\"your_key\")`.\n4. Verify the connection by calling the health check endpoint: `client.health_check()`.\n\n## Authentication Procedures\n- Store your API key securely using environment variables: `os.environ[\"API_KEY\"]`.\n- Inject the environment variable into the client initialization: `client = CloudScaleDataStream(api_key=os.environ[\"API_KEY\"])`.\n- Rotate your API keys every 90 days to maintain security compliance.\n- Use OAuth2 tokens for applications requiring multi-factor authentication.\n\n## Error Handling Strategies\n- Catch specific exceptions like `AuthenticationError` and `RateLimitExceeded`.\n- Implement exponential backoff for transient network",
